{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_framework", "label": "45-minute system design framework", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Requirements, non-functional targets, architecture, data flow, module design, deep dive, trade-offs. Scoping before solving and closing with what you gave up and how you would know it was wrong is the part most candidates skip and the most senior-sounding."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_caching_layers", "label": "Client-to-CDN caching stack", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Browser HTTP cache to CDN to app data cache to in-memory client cache; stale-while-revalidate is the single most useful header to mention, and on the client an LRU with TTL plus request dedup (LruCache and singleFlight in packages/core)."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_pagination", "label": "Offset vs cursor pagination", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offset is simple but breaks under concurrent inserts as rows shift and items duplicate or vanish; cursor/keyset is stable for infinite scroll and high-write tables but cannot jump to page 47."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_realtime_transport", "label": "Polling vs SSE vs WebSocket", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SSE is the cheapest correct answer for one-way feeds because it rides HTTP and auto-reconnects; choose WebSocket only when you need to write, since it needs its own scaling and backoff logic."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_resilience", "label": "Error handling and resilience", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Boundaries per route and per widget so one failure does not blank the page; retry with exponential backoff and jitter (retry() in packages/core); circuit-break a failing dependency; always offer a recovery affordance."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_problem_news_feed", "label": "Problem: news feed / infinite scroll", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cursor pagination, virtualisation, optimistic likes, prefetch n+1, scroll restoration from history state; the trap is unreserved image dimensions failing CLS."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_problem_typeahead", "label": "Problem: typeahead at scale", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Debounce 200-300 ms, cancel in flight, LRU cache by query prefix, minimum query length, dedup, keyboard support and aria-live count; the trap is the race condition, implemented twice in this repo."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_problem_collab_editor", "label": "Problem: collaborative editor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CRDT versus OT, WebSocket with presence, local-first via IndexedDB, and per-user undo; the trap is treating it as a save problem when it is a merge problem."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_problem_design_system", "label": "Problem: design system for many teams", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tokens to CSS custom properties to components on headless primitives so accessibility is not re-litigated per component; the trap is over-abstracting before three products' worth of real usage."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_problem_live_dashboard", "label": "Problem: dashboard with live data", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One multiplexed connection rather than twenty, per-widget Suspense and error boundaries, coalesced updates and server-side aggregation; the trap is re-rendering the whole grid on every tick."}, {"id": "docs_05_system_design_readme_problem_checkout", "label": "Problem: checkout / multi-step form", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "URL-driven steps, client validation for UX and server for truth, idempotency key on submit, draft persisted locally; optimistic UI is wrong here because payment needs a confirmed result."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_05_system_design_readme_framework", "target": "docs_05_system_design_readme_caching_layers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_05_system_design_readme_framework", "target": "docs_05_system_design_readme_pagination", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/05-system-design/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"so